    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d846">

                <pb facs="0805" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5151/860: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-09-24T23:00:00-04:00">September 24,
                            1941—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>612. Peiping’s despatch no. 3123, May 20, seizure of American relief funds from
                    Mr. Elmer W. Gait; despatch no. 36, June 18, seizure of American currency
                    belonging to Mr. M. H. Patton; and despatch no. 37, June 18, confiscation of
                    Chinese currency belonging to Mr. Bergman B. Lee.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d846-f1"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>The Department desires that the Embassy, if it perceives no objection and has not
                    already done so, make appropriate representations to the Foreign Office with
                    regard to these three cases involving seizure <pb facs="0806" n="796"
                        xml:id="pg796"/> of funds belonging to Americans and an American
                    organization by Japanese officials and by Japanese agents.<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d846-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Peiping. Repeated to Tientsin and Chungking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d846-f1" n="25" xml:id="d846-f1-content">
                <p>None printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d846-f2" n="30" xml:id="d846-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 1551, October 1, 10 a.m., Ambassador Grew reported to the
                    Department that appropriate representations were made to the Japanese Foreign
                    Office in a third-person note dated September 30 (893.5151/872).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
